    "GPU line: a queued GPU job that is ready except for the GPU joins the line; the worker starts a claim unit (simq-job-gpuclaim-<token12>.service) that waits for testing-gpu.lock in the kernel queue, takes testing-gpu-<UUID>.lock without blocking and hands both open files to the job unit over SCM_RIGHTS",
    "the job's time limit starts with its unit, after the GPU was won; a --gpu-mem job downgrades the received locks to shared",
    "line order by since time: a claim's is the exact submit time of its oldest ready job (birth time of the job log), a gpu-lease user's its start time; ties go to the queue",
    "raw flock waiters blocked on the GPU file ahead of a line member are moved to the tail of the kernel queue (SIGSTOP then SIGCONT, logged); requeue_commands default [flock]",
    "bin/gpu-lease [--core any|both|N] [--timeout S] [--label T] -- CMD: fair direct GPU use, GPU files first, then the core lease",
    "published state <pic-profile>/simq-gpu-line.json (schema simqueue-gpu-line-v1, heartbeat 10 s, withdrawn when the worker stops)",
    "simq partitions / sinfo / show / status / doctor show the GPU holder, the line, raw waiters and a starvation warning after 600 s",
    "claims survive worker restarts and upgrades and are adopted by the next worker",
